              Christopher",
  abstract = "Recent Iterated Response (IR) models of pragmatics conceptualize
              language use as a recursive process in which agents reason about
              each other to increase communicative efficiency. These models are
              generally defined over complete utterances. However, there is
              substantial evidence that pragmatic reasoning takes place
