  volume    =  600,
  pages     = "695--700",
  abstract  = "Surveys are a crucial tool for understanding public opinion and
               behaviour, and their accuracy depends on maintaining statistical
               representativeness of their target populations by minimizing
               biases from all sources. Increasing data size shrinks confidence
               intervals but magnifies the effect of survey bias: an instance of
