  number    =  10,
  pages     = "1391--1400",
  abstract  = "In the phenomenon of attentional blink, identical visual stimuli
               are sometimes fully perceived and sometimes not detected at all.
               This phenomenon thus provides an optimal situation to study the
               fate of stimuli not consciously perceived and the differences
               between conscious and nonconscious processing. We correlated
               behavioral visibility ratings and recordings of event-related
