  volume    =  41,
  number    =  13,
  pages     = "1728--1737",
  abstract  = "We show that populations of visually responsive cells in the
               anterior part of the superior temporal sulcus (STSa) of the
               macaque monkey code for the sight of both specific articulated
               body actions and the consequent articulated static body postures.
               We define articulated actions as actions where one body part
