               postures contain a torsion or rotation between parts, while
               non-articulated postures do not. Cells were tested with the sight
               of articulated and non-articulated actions followed by the
               resultant articulated or non-articulated static body postures. In
               addition, the static body postures that formed the start and end
               of the actions were tested in isolation. The cells studied did
