  volume    =  286,
  number    =  5445,
  pages     = "1692--1695",
  abstract  = "The ability to ``mentalize,'' that is to understand and
               manipulate other people's behavior in terms of their mental
               states, is a major ingredient in successful social interactions.
               A rudimentary form of this ability may be seen in great apes, but
               in humans it is developed to a high level. Specific impairments
