               in visual attention between groups was found as indicated by
               fixation duration and normalized fixation number on the presented
               stimuli. RESULTS: The mu suppression over the sensorimotor cortex
               was significantly affected by experimental conditions, but not by
               group membership, nor by the interaction between groups and
               conditions. Individuals with ASD, similar to the controls,
