  journal   = "Hum. Brain Mapp.",
  publisher = "Wiley",
  volume    =  33,
  number    =  9,
  pages     = "2238--2254",
  abstract  = "As humans, we gather a wide range of information about other
               people from watching them move. A network of parietal, premotor,
               and occipitotemporal regions within the human brain, termed the
               action observation network (AON), has been implicated in
               understanding others' actions by means of an automatic matching
