               induced, and once according to their color balance. The groups
               differed significantly on both alexithymia and empathy
               questionnaires. Alexithymia and lack of empathy were correlated,
               indicating a link between understanding one's own and others'
               emotions. For both groups a strong relationship between
               questionnaire scores and brain activity was found in the anterior
               insula (AI), when participants were required to assess their
