               neuropeptides. DesGly-NH(2)-d(CH(2))(5)-[D-Tyr(2),Thr(4)]OVT) for
               OT receptor, SR 49059 for V1a subtype receptor, and SSR-149415
               for V1b subtype receptor were injected i.m. 10 min before each
               agonist. RESULTS: All the peptides increased social preference
               and reduced fear to predator response in a dose-dependent manner
               interpolated by symmetrical parabolas. AVT/AVP were more potent
               to elicit anxiolytic than social effect while IT and OT were
