                   empirically study the effectiveness of our defense mechanisms
                   on two DNNs placed in adversarial settings. The study shows
                   that defensive distillation can reduce effectiveness of
                   sample creation from 95\% to less than 0.5\% on a studied
                   DNN. Such dramatic gains can be explained by the fact that
                   distillation leads gradients used in adversarial sample
                   creation to be reduced by a factor of 10\textasciicircum30.
                   We also find that distillation increases the average minimum
                   number of features that need to be modified to create
                   adversarial samples by about 800\% on one of the DNNs we
                   tested.",
  month         =  nov,
  year          =  2015,
  archivePrefix = "arXiv",
