  journal       = "arXiv [cs.NE]",
  abstract      = "When a large feedforward neural network is trained on a small
                   training set, it typically performs poorly on held-out test
                   data. This ``overfitting'' is greatly reduced by randomly
                   omitting half of the feature detectors on each training case.
                   This prevents complex co-adaptations in which a feature
