  number    =  2,
  pages     = "215--234",
  abstract  = "Generalized linear models play an essential role in a wide
               variety of statistical applications. This paper discusses an
               approximation of the likelihood in these models that can greatly
               facilitate computation. The basic idea is to replace a sum that
               appears in the exact log-likelihood by an expectation over the
