  volume    =  5,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "64--79",
  abstract  = "Many recent studies have shown that representations drawn from
               neural network language models are extremely effective at
               predicting brain responses to natural language. But why do these
               models work so well? One proposed explanation is that language
               models and brains are similar because they have the same
               objective: to predict upcoming words before they are perceived.
