  pages     =  555,
  abstract  = "A key sticking point of Bayesian analysis is the choice of prior
               distribution, and there is a vast literature on potential
               defaults including uniform priors, Jeffreys’ priors, reference
               priors, maximum entropy priors, and weakly informative priors.
               These methods, however, often manifest a key conceptual tension
