  journal  = "J. Neurosci.",
  volume   =  30,
  number   =  32,
  pages    = "10744--10751",
  abstract = "Humans have the arguably unique ability to understand the mental
              representations of others. For success in both competitive and
              cooperative interactions, however, this ability must be extended
              to include representations of others' belief about our intentions,
              their model about our belief about their intentions, and so on. We
