  volume    =  5,
  number    =  1178450,
  pages     =  1178450,
  abstract  = "Recently, a considerable number of studies in computer vision
               involve deep neural architectures called vision transformers.
               Visual processing in these models incorporates computational
               models that are claimed to implement attention mechanisms.
               Despite an increasing body of work that attempts to understand
               the role of attention mechanisms in vision transformers, their
               effect is largely unknown. Here, we asked if the attention
               mechanisms in vision transformers exhibit similar effects as
               those known in human visual attention. To answer this question,
               we revisited the attention formulation in these models and found
               that despite the name, computationally, these models perform a
