  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  86,
  number    =  102866,
  pages     =  102866,
  abstract  = "A variety of organisms exhibit collective movement, including
               schooling fish and flocking birds, where coordinated behavior
               emerges from the interactions between group members. Despite the
               prevalence of collective movement in nature, little is known
               about the neural mechanisms producing each individual's behavior
