  publisher = "Association for Computational Linguistics",
  address   = "Stroudsburg, PA, USA",
  abstract  = "Scripts representing common sense knowledge about stereotyped
               sequences of events have been shown to be a valuable resource for
               NLP applications. We present a hierarchical Bayesian model for
               unsupervised learning of script knowledge from crowdsourced
               descriptions of human activities. Events and constraints on event
               ordering are induced jointly in one unified framework. We use a
               statistical model over permutations which captures event ordering
