  publisher = "scholarworks.smith.edu",
  abstract  = "Scripts, knowledge structures defining sequences of events in
               stereotypical social situations, were traditionally used to
               simulate the ways in which people can infer unstated details in
               understanding a story. In this paper, we describe the MUltiple
               SCRipt AcTivator (MUSCRAT), and the Script Combination Applier
               Mechanism (SCAM), significant enhancements of Cullingford’s
               Script Applier Mechanism which accomplish two novel aims. One
               system, MUSCRAT, is able to activate more than one script and use
               them during a story understanding process. The second system,
               SCAM, uses scripts for story generation, using script variables
