  pages     = "327--339",
  abstract  = "The authors propose that people adopt others' perspectives by
               serially adjusting from their own. As predicted, estimates of
               others' perceptions were consistent with one's own but differed
               in a manner consistent with serial adjustment (Study 1).
               Participants were slower to indicate that another's perception
               would be different from--rather than similar to--their own (Study
